+### 10.5 Implementation profiles and application composition
+
+`DIR-PROFILE-001` — Maintain three distinct layers: this normative standard; implementation profiles under existing accepted responsibility owners; and a commit-pinned, non-normative current-state inventory. Profiles explain conventions without expanding root authority. Inventory updates do not accept architecture, commission features, admit sources, or promote data. Reuse existing requirement/capability and verification identities rather than creating a competing registry.
+
+`DIR-DEP-004` — Deployable applications may own feature state, views, controllers, authentication helpers, workers, and framework-required platform files. Reusable packages shall expose explicit independently testable interfaces when genuine shared use or an independently justified boundary exists. Do not extract merely for symmetry, import another application's internals, or create catch-all ownership. Keep capabilities host-independent where practical; provider configuration does not justify a responsibility root or hosting migration.
+
+The candidate [implementation profiles](../architecture/directory-implementation-profiles.md) and [pinned inventory](../architecture/directory-current-state-20260905.md) accompany ADR-0039. Their presence while proposed does not amend the existing authority.
+
+### 10.6 Build and export input contracts
+
+`DIR-BUILD-001` — Each supported build/deployment entrypoint shall identify the edited source tree, framework entrypoints, public package interfaces, source aliases, installer/version, manifest and consumed lockfile, assembly procedure, generated inputs, builder input boundary, and excluded content. Trace aliases into sibling source packages. Preserve installer inputs with demonstrated consumers and the existing dependency build-script allow/deny policy.
+
+`DIR-BUILD-002` — An app-only export shall contain its permitted build dependencies or have a tested assembly process supplying them. Missing sibling packages shall fail explicitly rather than trigger CDN/global renderer acquisition or silent synthetic fallback. Preserve the package-owned MapLibre boundary, including workers, styles, plugins, and protocols. A minimum-file check does not prove transitive closure; test the intended assembled context without deploying.
+
+`DIR-BUILD-003` — Bundle selection shall distinguish runtime demonstrations, test-only inputs, generated assets, durable receipts/proofs, released data, secrets, internal stores, and disposable output. Copy rules shall not promote test fixtures or unadmitted data into released artifacts. Preserve fixture/model/observation disclosure and applicable rights, sensitivity, mutability, retention, correction, and rollback obligations. A manifest or successful build is not source admission or release approval.
+
+### 10.7 Verification placement and evidence
+
+`DIR-TEST-001` — App/package-local unit and component tests may colocate with their owned behavior under existing permitted conventions. Repository-wide contract, schema, policy, integration, and end-to-end checks retain explicit shared ownership. Public-safe shared fixtures and private fixtures shall declare ownership, permitted reuse, discovery, and exposure. A moved test must remain discoverable, non-vacuous, connected to its intended target and CI entrypoint, and excluded from inappropriate application bundles.
+
+`DIR-TEST-002` — Trace stable requirement/capability identities through user outcomes, app surfaces, public functions/types/commands/APIs, contracts/schemas/policies, fixtures/tests, CI, acceptance criteria, and correction/rollback dependencies. Mark missing implementation, dormant integration, missing tests, unrun checks, fixture proof, runtime proof, deployment, and release separately. Do not hand-maintain every private function or report placeholder root commands as successful validation.
+
+`DIR-TEST-003` — Changed-area checks shall address applicable denied/restricted data, stale evidence, malformed imports, unsupported time, interrupted frame changes, missing packages, and absent renderer capabilities. Preserve local-import privacy, redaction in URLs/logs/exports, finite Focus outcomes, report reproducibility, and valid/observed/retrieval/release-time distinctions. Assert expected negative diagnostics and state invariants, not any nonzero exit. Record command, revision/tree, toolchain, exit and actual result; use comparable same-base evidence before calling a failure inherited. Browser/GPU, worker/CSS, keyboard/mobile/accessibility, visual/performance, and long-session results prove only their tested behavior; an in-memory host cannot certify rendering or public operation.
